ents may be identified in multiple complexity categories simultaneously.\n\n"],"source_url":"https://open.alberta.ca/dataset/e3d5e3e2-fd4c-457c-b39a-e77118e7de7c/resource/41f8b7df-d23e-4e23-b4c2-6f2440d39ef2/download/ecc-alberta-class-size-2025-2026.xlsx","catalogue_url":"https://open.alberta.ca/opendata/alberta-class-size","sha256":"40be6316611bb3152d82011d8a86373992165e94bff1037e694954e738e417e4","method":"One published row per teacher and unique student group for a portion of instructional time. Students can recur across rows. Suppressed sizes are 1–9 and therefore below both OECD cutoffs; they remain in denominators. Excludes alternative, outreach/online and special-purpose schools and special-education subjects. Not a census of every Alberta classroom. No historical series is inferred."}
